../CLAUDE.md-146-### Shell sandbox
../CLAUDE.md-147-
../CLAUDE.md:148:`engine/sandbox.rs` confines the `bash` tool's writes to the workspace, `/tmp` and this user's `$TMPDIR`, the data-only cache subdirs in `HOME_CACHES` and `CACHE_ENV` (never `~/.cargo/bin`, `~/.rustup` or the npx cache), and an out-of-root git dir. The git control paths in `GIT_CONTROL` (hooks, config, `config.worktree`, `commondir`) and the `.git` entry stay read-only inside those trees, for the shell and for `write_file`/`edit_file`. Every git command slag runs itself goes through `sandbox::git()` / `git_async()`, which add `-c core.hooksPath=/dev/null -c core.fsmonitor=false`; never call `Command::new("git")` directly. `sandbox::protect_git_dir` locks slag's private repos (the `slag fix` shadow). Landlock cannot lock a file inside a writable tree, so `git_guard` records the program-running config keys when a sandbox first covers a repo and `git()` refuses once they change. Reads and network stay open. `ToolBox` resolves it at the first shell call; `bash`, `grep`, `glob`, and background jobs all run under it. `proof::run_shell_in` runs proofs and CMD lines (forge and duel) in it, and `fix::repo::run` runs every `slag fix` test command in it, because the model writes or can edit both. Hooks, `screenshot_cmd` and `[mcp]` servers stay outside: the user wrote them. Every other spawn is either a fixed binary with fixed arguments (`tar`, `kill`, `uname`, `gh` with `GIT_GUARD_ENV`, guarded `git`) or runs through `Sandbox::wrap`/`wrap_std`; anything whose program, script or import the workspace controls (test detection's `imports()` probe included) must take the sandbox.
../CLAUDE.md-149-
../CLAUDE.md-150-| Setting | Env | `config.toml` key | Flag |
../CLAUDE.md-151-|---------|-----|-------------------|------|
--
../CLAUDE.md-154-
../CLAUDE.md-155-Backends: macOS runs `sandbox-exec` with a generated Seatbelt profile. Linux uses `bwrap` when it works, else Landlock (raw syscalls, no crate), else runs unconfined. `main.rs` calls `sandbox::preflight()` before the dashboard starts, which prints one warning per run when nothing can confine writes. A refused write adds `write outside the workspace was blocked by slag's sandbox: <path>` to the tool result, leads a failed proof's output, and rides on a fix test run's `status()`.
../CLAUDE.md-156-
../CLAUDE.md:157:Other environment knobs include `SLAG_DUEL`, `SLAG_DUEL_ROUNDS`, `SLAG_REASONING_EFFORT`, `SLAG_SCREENSHOT_CMD`, `SLAG_CONFIG_DIR`, and `SLAG_CHAR_BUDGET` (agent compaction budget). `tui.rs` also reads `NO_COLOR` and `COLORTERM`.
../CLAUDE.md-158-
../CLAUDE.md-159-Behavior constants in `config.rs`: `MAX_ANVILS = 3` (parallel ingot slots), `HIGH_GRADE = 3` (plan-model threshold), `MAX_ITERATE = 3` (self-iteration rounds).
../CLAUDE.md-160-
../CLAUDE.md:161:`DuelMode::Auto` duels grade 3 and up, and only when `model_alt` differs from `model_base`. With everything on `openrouter/auto` that gate stays shut, so the default never pays 3x tokens to duel a model against itself.
